From: Local integration <local@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] cpuidle: avoid idle entry with a pending local call-function IPI

Backport the per-CPU pending-IPI check proposed by Maulik Shah:
https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260403-cpuidle_ipi-v2-1-b3e44b032e2c@oss.qualcomm.com

Keep the helper call inside instrumentation_begin/end: placing an instrumented
function call before instrumentation_begin in noinstr code is invalid. Check
only the current CPU, not the entire driver's mask. This is a best-effort
snapshot, not a guarantee that no new interrupt can arrive after the check.

--- a/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle.c
+++ b/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle.c
@@ -222,6 +222,11 @@ noinstr int cpuidle_enter_state(struct cpuidle_device *dev,
 
 	instrumentation_begin();
 
+	if (cpus_peek_for_pending_ipi(cpumask_of(dev->cpu))) {
+		instrumentation_end();
+		return -EBUSY;
+	}
+
 	/*
 	 * The vendor hook may modify index, which means target_state and
 	 * broadcast must be assigned after the vendor hook.
